# Schema: Polkadot SDK PRDoc Schema (prdoc) v1.0.0
# See doc at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/paritytech/polkadot-sdk/master/prdoc/schema_user.json

title: Remove XCM v3

doc:
  - audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
    description: |
      XCM v3 is removed. The minimum supported version is now v4: `xcm::v3`, the `V3`
      variants of all `Versioned*` types, `AlwaysV3` and `VersionedLocatableAsset::V3`
      are gone. Types that v4 and v5 re-exported from v3 (`Error`, `SendError`, `XcmHash`,
      `BodyId`, `BodyPart`, `OriginKind`, `WeightLimit`, ...) now live in `xcm::v4`, which
      renames their metadata type paths.

      v4 and v5 encodings are unchanged, but v3-encoded data can no longer be decoded.
      Before upgrading, chains must have run `pallet_xcm::migration::MigrateToLatestXcmVersion`
      and migrated any own storage holding v3 types. Assets trapped under a v3 hash become
      unclaimable and v3-only destinations become unreachable.

crates:
  - name: staging-xcm
    bump: major
  - name: xcm-procedural
    bump: major
  - name: pallet-xcm
    bump: minor
  - name: polkadot-runtime-common
    bump: major
  - name: parachains-common
    bump: patch
  - name: staging-xcm-builder
    bump: minor
  - name: pallet-xcm-precompiles
    bump: none
  - name: xcm-runtime-apis
    bump: none
  - name: asset-hub-rococo-runtime
    bump: major
  - name: asset-test-utils
    bump: patch
  - name: snowbridge-pallet-inbound-queue
    bump: minor
  - name: cumulus-pallet-xcmp-queue
    bump: none
  - name: pallet-contracts-uapi
    bump: none
